  <p class="eyebrow">Guide · Sourcing</p>
  <h1>Telegram vs Alibaba for peptides</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Alibaba is cheaper per gram and worse per order. Both statements are true at once, and which one matters
    depends on whether you are buying one vial or fifty.
  </p>

  <h2>Where Alibaba wins</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Unit price at volume. Fifty vials direct from a Chinese factory is a fraction of any EU price.</li>
    <li>Custom synthesis, if you want something nobody stocks.</li>
    <li>Bulk raw powder, if you are comfortable weighing and capping.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where Alibaba loses</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Minimum order. One vial is not a viable Alibaba order once shipping is on it.</li>
    <li>Time. Two to five weeks, and customs is a real risk on a commercial-value parcel.</li>
    <li>COA quality. Many listings attach a generic COA that belongs to no specific batch, or a different product.</li>
    <li>Recourse. A dispute on a 40 dollar order is not worth the hours.</li>
    <li>No reship. A seized Alibaba parcel is your loss, in practice.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The COA problem specifically</h2>
  <p>
    A factory COA is an in-house document. An independent COA is a different thing. Most Alibaba listings offer
    the first and describe it as the second. If you go that route, budget for testing one vial from the batch
    yourself before committing to volume — the test costs more than the vial and less than a bad batch.
  </p>

  <h2>The break-even</h2>
  <p>
    Roughly ten vials. Under ten, the shipping, the wait and the customs exposure eat the saving. Over ten, and
    if you already know the molecule and the lab, Alibaba is genuinely cheaper. Between one and ten, a Telegram
    desk at 18 to 26 with a batch COA and a reship policy is the better trade.
  </p>

  <h2>What people actually do</h2>
  <p>
    Buy one vial from a desk to confirm the product is what you expect, then go to Alibaba for volume if the
    molecule suits you. Or stay on the desk for the convenience and pay the small premium. Both are rational.
  </p>

